        <briefdescription>
<para>Linearly interpolate UT1 - UTC between two tabulated values. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>UT1 - UTC jumps by +1 s across a leap second, while UT1 - TAI is continuous. Interpolating UT1 - UTC directly spreads that jump over the whole day that ends with the leap second. Across a leap second, UT1 - TAI is interpolated instead and converted back to UT1 - UTC with TAI - UTC at the requested instant.</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">double<sp/>ut1MinusUtc<sp/>=<sp/>utilities::interpolateUt1MinusUtc(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>previousUt1MinusUtc,<sp/>previousMjd_UTC,<sp/>nextUt1MinusUtc,<sp/>nextMjd_UTC,<sp/>ratio,<sp/>instant</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
